@moduledoc """
Where your application reacts to events.

`handle/1` receives the decoded envelope (a map with string keys: `"id"`,
`"type"`, `"occurred_at"`, `"payload"`) and returns:

  * `:ok` - handled, acknowledge it;
  * `:skip` - not interested, acknowledge it;
  * `{:error, reason}` - failed, JetStream redelivers it.

Pattern-match on `"type"`:

    def handle(%{"type" => "organization.create", "payload" => payload}) do
      # …
      :ok
    end

    def handle(_event), do: :skip

Delivery is at-least-once, so handlers must be idempotent; `"id"` is stable
across redeliveries.
"""

require Logger

@spec handle(map()) :: :ok | :skip | {:error, term()}
def handle(%{"type" => type, "id" => id}) do
  Logger.info("event #{type} (#{id})")
  :ok
end

def handle(_event), do: :skip
